  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.8pt, 90.28pt, "Operational entanglement of collective quantum modes at room temperature ")
  #line-at(224.85pt, 119.55pt, "Shalender Singh*")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.88pt, 119.55pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.38pt, 119.55pt, "Santosh Kumar ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.6pt, 132.05pt, "PolariQon Inc., Palo Alto, California, USA")
  #line-at(267.35pt, 144.8pt, "(December 2025)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(285.63pt, 170.05pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 182.8pt, "Quantum entanglement is commonly assumed to be fragile at ambient temperature and over macroscopic ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 195.33pt, "distances, where thermal noise and dissipation are expected to rapidly suppress nonclassical correlations. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 208.08pt, "Here we show that this intuition fails for collective quantum modes whose dynamics is governed by ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 220.83pt, "reduced open-system channels rather than by microscopic thermal equilibrium. For two spatially ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 233.33pt, "separated collective modes, we derive an exact entanglement boundary based on the positivity of the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 246.08pt, "partial transpose, valid in the symmetric resonant limit. From this result we obtain an ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0e0e0e"))
  #line-at(449.45pt, 246.08pt, "explicit")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(482.45pt, 246.08pt, " minimum ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 258.58pt, "collective fluctuation amplitude, expressed entirely in measurable noise, bandwidth, dissipation, and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 271.33pt, "distance-dependent coupling parameters, required to sustain steady-state entanglement at finite ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 284.1pt, "temperature. We further show that large collective occupation suppresses but does not eliminate quantum ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 296.6pt, "phase diffusion, so the steady state remains phase symmetric and does not collapse to a classical mean-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 309.35pt, "field despite macroscopic signal amplitudes. Stochastic simulations of the reduced open-system ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 321.85pt, "dynamics, together with matched classical correlated-noise null models analyzed through an identical ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 334.6pt, "pipeline, confirm that entanglement witnesses are violated only in the quantum regime. Our results ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 347.35pt, "establish a minimal, platform-independent framework connecting collective-mode dynamics, noise ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 359.87pt, "injection, distance, and operational certification of macroscopic entanglement.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 385.12pt, "1. INTRODUCTION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 411.87pt, "Quantum entanglement is widely regarded as fragile at ambient temperature and over macroscopic ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 424.37pt, "distances, where thermal noise and environmental decoherence are expected to rapidly suppress ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 437.15pt, "nonclassical correlations. This intuition is well founded for microscopic degrees of freedom whose ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 449.9pt, "dynamics is directly governed by local dissipation and thermal equilibrium with a surrounding bath [1,2]. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 462.4pt, "In such systems, increasing temperature or spatial separation typically leads to rapid loss of coherence and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 475.15pt, "entanglement. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 501.65pt, "However, a growing body of experimental and theoretical work has demonstrated that macroscopic ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 514.42pt, "quantum phenomena can persist when the relevant degrees of freedom are collective rather than ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 527.17pt, "microscopic [3–6]. In systems supporting macroscopic order parameters—such as Bose–Einstein ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 539.67pt, "condensates and related coherent many-body states—the physically relevant quantum variables are ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 552.42pt, "collective modes describing slow amplitude and phase fluctuations of the order parameter [3,7–9]. These ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 564.92pt, "modes can exhibit large occupation numbers and macroscopic signal amplitudes while retaining ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 577.67pt, "intrinsically quantum features, including phase diffusion and nonclassical correlations. Crucially, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 590.45pt, "increasing ensemble size does not generically force a collective mode into a classical or mean-field ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 602.95pt, "description; instead, it suppresses relative fluctuations while leaving global quantum uncertainty intact ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 615.7pt, "[4,8–10]. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 642.2pt, "Recent reports have described quantum signatures—including inseparability witnesses and long-range ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 654.95pt, "correlations—in systems operating at room temperature, with large measured signal amplitudes and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 667.7pt, "spatial separations far exceeding typical microscopic coherence lengths [11–14]. At first sight, such ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 680.47pt, "observations appear to conflict with the conventional expectation that thermal energy ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(449.95pt, 680.47pt, "𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(455.95pt, 682.72pt, "𝐵")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(462.2pt, 680.47pt, "𝑇")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(468.95pt, 680.47pt, " necessarily ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 693.225pt, "destroys quantum coherence. This apparent contradiction arises from implicitly treating the relevant ")
]

