  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.58pt, 108.03pt, "𝑇/ℏ𝜔")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(203.33pt, 108.03pt, ". ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 134.8pt, "2.5 Physical interpretation")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 161.3pt, "The entanglement criterion derived above admits a transparent physical interpretation once the distinction ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 174.05pt, "between mean-field order and quantum collective fluctuations is made explicit. In systems with large ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 187.55pt, "ensemble participation, the expectation value of the collective mode operator ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(413.92pt, 187.55pt, "⟨Ψ̂⟩")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.43pt, 187.55pt, " may acquire a large ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 200.08pt, "magnitude, corresponding to a macroscopic order parameter or coherent amplitude. This quantity behaves ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 214.58pt, "classically in the sense that relative fluctuations scale as ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(321.13pt, 214.58pt, "1/√𝑁")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(348.15pt, 214.58pt, ", and its dynamics is well captured by ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 227.33pt, "mean-field equations. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 253.83pt, "Crucially, however, the existence of a large mean-field amplitude does not imply that the collective mode ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 267.33pt, "itself becomes classical. The quantum state of the collective degree of freedom is encoded not in ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(499.45pt, 267.33pt, "⟨Ψ̂⟩")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(515.97pt, 267.33pt, ", but ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 280.1pt, "in the fluctuations of its conjugate quadratures and their correlations. These quantum collective ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 292.85pt, "fluctuations remain governed by canonical commutation relations independently of ensemble size and are ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 305.6pt, "fully characterized by the covariance matrix of the reduced open system. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 332.1pt, "Noise processes acting on individual constituents predominantly excite modes orthogonal to the collective ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 344.85pt, "subspace and therefore do not directly decohere the collective quantum fluctuations. As a result, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 357.37pt, "increasing ensemble size suppresses relative amplitude noise and enhances signal-to-noise ratios of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 370.12pt, "collective observables, while leaving the global phase subject to quantum diffusion rather than classical ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 382.62pt, "pinning. This behavior is well known from the theory of lasers and Bose–Einstein condensates, where ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 395.37pt, "macroscopic occupation coexists with intrinsically quantum phase dynamics. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 422.12pt, "In this framework, steady-state entanglement arises from correlations between the quantum collective ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 434.65pt, "fluctuations of spatially separated modes, not from the mean-field order parameter itself. The persistence ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 447.4pt, "of entanglement at large ensemble size therefore does not represent a violation of decoherence intuition, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 459.9pt, "but a direct consequence of the separation between mean-field behavior and quantum collective dynamics ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 472.65pt, "in open many-body systems. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 503.4pt, "2.6 Analytical application: minimum collective amplitude for robust entanglement ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 529.92pt, "In this section we apply the general collective-mode theory developed above to a minimal analytical ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 542.67pt, "setting in order to determine the conditions under which steady-state entanglement can be sustained and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 555.17pt, "certified in the presence of ambient noise. The purpose of this analysis is not to introduce new physical ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 568.17pt, "assumptions, but to connect the abstract open-system parameters ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(359.65pt, 567.67pt, "(𝐺")
  #line-at(371.65pt, 564.92pt, ", ")
  #line-at(375.65pt, 568.17pt, "𝜅")
  #line-at(381.9pt, 564.92pt, ", ")
