  #line-at(246.85pt, 132.05pt, "Fig. 4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(273.13pt, 132.05pt, ", where the Duan–Simon witness approaches its asymptotic ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 145.05pt, "value with increasing ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(168.83pt, 145.05pt, "𝑇𝐵")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(182.83pt, 145.05pt, ". Importantly, the entanglement threshold itself is independent of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(470.95pt, 145.05pt, "𝑇")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(477.7pt, 145.05pt, "and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(496.45pt, 145.05pt, "𝐵")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(503.95pt, 145.05pt, ", ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 157.55pt, "confirming that these parameters affect only statistical confidence rather than the existence of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 170.3pt, "entanglement. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 197.08pt, "3.6 Summary of results")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 223.58pt, "Together, the results in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.33pt, 223.58pt, "Figs. 1–4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(217.85pt, 223.58pt, " validate the analytical predictions of Section 2 and establish a clear ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 236.33pt, "operational distinction between collective quantum entanglement and classical correlated noise. The ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 248.83pt, "collective-mode Lindblad model exhibits steady-state entanglement precisely where predicted by the PPT ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 261.58pt, "criterion, while none of the classical null models reproduce the same inseparability under identical ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 274.35pt, "analysis conditions. These findings demonstrate that macroscopic, room-temperature entanglement of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 286.85pt, "collective modes is a genuine consequence of reduced open-system quantum dynamics rather than a ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 299.6pt, "measurement or noise artifact. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 326.35pt, "4. DISCUSSION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 352.85pt, "The analysis presented in Sections 2 and 3 establishes a clear separation between the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(447.43pt, 352.85pt, "existence of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 365.62pt, "entanglement as a property of the collective quantum state")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(346.65pt, 365.62pt, " and the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.15pt, 365.62pt, "operational ability to certify that ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 378.12pt, "entanglement under realistic measurement constraints")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327.63pt, 378.12pt, ". This separation resolves several apparent ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 390.87pt, "paradoxes surrounding long-distance, room-temperature entanglement in macroscopic systems and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 403.62pt, "clarifies the role of ensemble size, temperature, and signal amplitude. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 430.12pt, "4.1 Collective modes and the absence of mean-field collapse ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 456.9pt, "A central result of this work is that large ensemble participation does not, by itself, force a collective ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 469.4pt, "quantum mode into a classical or mean-field description. As shown in Section 2, the relevant degrees of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 482.15pt, "freedom are collective envelope modes whose reduced dynamics is governed by an open-system ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 494.65pt, "description. Microscopic decoherence processes predominantly populate modes orthogonal to this ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 507.4pt, "collective subspace, while the collective mode itself couples to its environment through a restricted set of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 520.42pt, "channels characterized by effective parameters ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(280.63pt, 519.92pt, "(𝐺")
  #line-at(292.63pt, 517.17pt, ", ")
  #line-at(296.88pt, 520.42pt, "𝜅")
  #line-at(303.13pt, 517.17pt, ", ")
  #line-at(307.13pt, 520.42pt, "𝑛")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.38pt, 522.67pt, "eff")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(323.88pt, 519.92pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(328.38pt, 520.42pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 546.92pt, "Importantly, the collective phase associated with this mode is not statically pinned. Instead, it undergoes ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 559.67pt, "quantum phase diffusion, with a diffusion constant that decreases with increasing collective occupation ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 572.17pt, "but remains finite. As a result, large ensemble size enhances signal amplitude and slows phase diffusion ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 584.93pt, "without eliminating quantum uncertainty. This behavior is fully consistent with standard quantum ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 597.45pt, "mechanics and mirrors the physics of lasers and condensates, where macroscopic occupation coexists ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 610.2pt, "with genuinely quantum collective fluctuations. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 636.95pt, "4.2 Distance enters only through the coherent coupling ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 663.45pt, "The theory makes explicit that spatial separation affects entanglement only through the coherent coupling ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 676.47pt, "rate ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(91.3pt, 676.47pt, "𝐺(𝑑)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.55pt, 676.47pt, " mediating interactions between collective modes. No additional distance-dependent ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 688.98pt, "decoherence term appears at the level of the reduced collective dynamics. Consequently, entanglement ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 701.725pt, "does not generically decay exponentially with distance unless such decay is present in the coupling ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 714.475pt, "channel itself. ")
]

