#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-16.png", width: 32.5pt), 310.5pt, 322pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 82.28pt, "This distinction is crucial: long-distance robustness is not a consequence of suppressing environmental ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 94.78pt, "noise, but of the fact that the collective mode remains the relevant quantum degree of freedom over ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 107.78pt, "macroscopic separations. The functional form of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(288.63pt, 107.78pt, "𝐺(𝑑)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(311.88pt, 107.78pt, " depends on geometry and mediation mechanism, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 120.55pt, "but once ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(112.3pt, 120.55pt, "𝐺(𝑑)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(135.55pt, 120.55pt, " is specified or measured, the entanglement condition follows directly from the open-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 133.3pt, "system parameters. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 160.05pt, "While the present framework is intentionally platform independent, the strong-coupling regime required ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 172.55pt, "for collective-mode entanglement is known to be accessible in several experimentally mature settings. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 185.3pt, "These include low-loss microwave or phononic waveguides, high-Q electromechanical and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 197.83pt, "optomechanical resonators, and magnonic systems where collective excitations couple coherently over ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 210.58pt, "macroscopic distances with dissipation rates well below the interaction strength. In such systems, the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 223.58pt, "reduced collective parameters ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(206.08pt, 223.58pt, "𝐺")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(213.6pt, 223.58pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.1pt, 223.58pt, "𝜅")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(225.35pt, 223.58pt, ", and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.6pt, 223.58pt, "𝑛")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.85pt, 225.83pt, "𝑒𝑓𝑓")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(270.63pt, 223.58pt, "entering our analysis can be independently engineered and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 237.58pt, "characterized. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 264.32pt, "4.3 Voltage thresholds and thermal noise ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 290.85pt, "The analytical application in Section 2.6 shows that the minimum collective fluctuation required to ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 303.6pt, "sustain steady-state entanglement scales as ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(267.35pt, 344.35pt, "𝑉")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(272.88pt, 346.6pt, "min")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.38pt, 344.35pt, "∝√")
  #line-at(312.38pt, 336.1pt, "𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(318.38pt, 338.35pt, "𝐵")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324.63pt, 336.1pt, "𝑇")
  #line-at(333.4pt, 336.1pt, "𝐵")
  #line-at(310.63pt, 351.6pt, "𝐶")
  #line-at(319.38pt, 351.6pt, "𝐺(𝑑)")
  #line-at(342.65pt, 344.35pt, ".")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 383.12pt, "This result highlights that ambient temperature enters only through effective noise injected into the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 395.87pt, "collective mode within the measurement bandwidth. Thermal energy at the microscopic scale does not ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 408.62pt, "directly set the entanglement threshold. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 435.15pt, "From this perspective, voltage (or more generally collective amplitude) plays an operational role: it ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 447.65pt, "increases the signal-to-noise ratio of the collective degree of freedom relative to injected noise. Once the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 460.4pt, "threshold is exceeded, entanglement exists as a steady-state property of the reduced system, independent ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 473.15pt, "of measurement duration. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 499.65pt, "4.4 Estimator-limited coherence and certification times ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 526.42pt, "Section 3 demonstrates that experimentally inferred “coherence times” or “entanglement lifetimes” in ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 538.92pt, "macroscopic systems are often limited by estimator statistics rather than by the underlying quantum state. ")
